      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "### GeneScale CRISPR Grant - Gene Editing Methodology\n\n#### Objective\nUtilize an AAV9 viral vector to deliver the Cas9 protein and guide RNA, targeting the HBB gene mutation to study the resulting genetic modifications and their effects.\n\n#### Methodology\n\n1. **Vector Delivery**: The AAV9 viral vector will be engineered to include the Cas9 nuclease gene and a meticulously designed guide RNA sequence, specifically targeting the mutation within the HBB gene.\n\n2. **Target Engagement**: The Cas9 protein, guided by the targeted RNA, will seek out the HBB gene mutation and facilitate site-specific double-strand breaks within the genomic DNA of the target cells.\n\n3. **Validation**:\n   - **Genetic Confirmation**: Employ confirmatory DNA sequencing to identify successful edits at the HBB locus accurately.\n   - **Protein Level Analysis**: Measure resulting hemoglobin synthesis levels through quantitative protein assays, ensuring that corrected gene function is achieved.\n\nBy meticulously following this methodological framework, we aim to validate the precise, targeted editing of the HBB gene, thereby effectively reducing the risks associated with off-target effects and maximizing the efficiency of our gene-editing approach. These rigorous validation steps are paramount to the success and credibility",
      "source": "target",
